---
import { SITE_URL, links } from "~/content/site";
import Article from "~/layouts/Article.astro";
---

<Article
	title="Terms of use"
	description="The terms that apply to this site and to downloading Brainstorm."
	eyebrow="Legal"
	date={new Date("2026-07-28")}
	localized={false}
>
	<p>
		These terms cover your use of <a href={SITE_URL}>{SITE_URL}</a> and the Brainstorm
		software you can download from it. They are short because the product is open source and
		the site asks almost nothing of you.
	</p>

	<h2>The software</h2>
	<p>
		Brainstorm is free and open source, licensed under the
		<a
			href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html"
			rel="noopener noreferrer">GNU AGPL-3.0</a
		>. The license — not this page — governs your rights to use, modify, and redistribute it.
		Brainstorm is pre-1.0 software under active development: it is provided "as is", without
		warranty of any kind, and we recommend keeping backups of anything important. Your data
		stays on your machine; if you enable sync, it is end-to-end encrypted.
	</p>

	<h2>The site</h2>
	<p>
		The content of this site (text, images, the Brainstorm name and mark) belongs to the
		Brainstorm project. You may link to it and quote it with attribution. Don't
		misrepresent the project, impersonate it, or use the site to do anything unlawful —
		including abusing the waitlist form.
	</p>

	<h2>Third-party links</h2>
	<p>
		The site links out to GitHub, YouTube, and the launch directories we are listed on. Those
		sites have their own terms and privacy practices; we are not responsible for them.
	</p>

	<h2>Liability</h2>
	<p>
		To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Brainstorm project is not liable for damages
		arising from your use of this site or the software. Nothing in these terms limits rights
		that consumer law grants you and that cannot be waived.
	</p>

	<h2>Changes and contact</h2>
	<p>
		If these terms change, the date above changes with it. Questions go to
		<a href="mailto:hello@getbrainstorm.online">hello@getbrainstorm.online</a> or an issue on
		<a href={links.github} rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>. See also the
		<a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
	</p>
</Article>
